Pumpkin Apple Streusel Muffins
  --Jan Sticka
  
2 1/2 c ap flour
2 1/4 c sugar, divided
1 tbsp pumpkin pie spice
1 tsp baking soda
1/2 tsp salt
1 c canned pumpkin purée
1/2 c vegetable oil
2 large eggs, lightly beaten
2 c peeled, cored, and chopped apple
2 tbsp ap flour
1/2 tsp ground cinnamon
4 tsp butter

Preheat the oven to 350 F (175 C). Grease 18 muffin cups or line cups with paper liners. Sift 2 1/2 c flour, 2 c sugar, pumpkin pie spice, baking soda, and salt together into a bowl. Combine pumpkin purée, oil, and eggs in a separate bowl; stir into flour mixture until batter is just moistened. Fold in apples. Divide batter among the prepared muffin cups, filling each to the top. Whisk remaining 1/4 c sugar, 2 tbsp flour, and cinnamon together in a bowl; cut in butter with 2 knives or a pastry blender until mixture resembles coarse crumbs. Sprinkle cinnamon topping evenly over muffin batter. Bake in the preheated oven until a toothpick inserted into muffins comes out clean, 35-40 min.


Notes: diy pumpkin pie spice: 1 1/2 tsp cinnamon, 3/4 tsp ginger, scant 1/2 tsp allspice, scant 1/2 tsp nutmeg. Might want to cut sugar in half. Add nuts
